{"name": "Piranha Restaurant & Sushi Bar", "address": "714 State St", "city": "Santa Barbara", "state": "CA", "categories": "Restaurants, Sushi Bars", "hours": null, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": false, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": null, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "Music": null, "Ambience": null}, "business_stars": 3.0, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2008-08-08 19:51:46", "review_text": "The sushi was mediocre but I still like the environment and the service!"}, {"review_stars": 2.0, "review_date": "2008-07-26 05:03:21", "review_text": ""after a lovely day at the beach, my husband and i decided to finish off the day with some sushi. we'd eaten at piranha before and enjoyed it, but after tonight's experience, i can safely say we will never return. it wasn't heinous--but for 80$, the quality of the food and service was pretty abysmal. not only was the sushi NOT super fresh and tasty, especially as compared to katsuya in encino, but the waitstaff was inattentive (we had to call out for the hostess finally to get our waitress's attention), the waitress made a mistake on our order and did not recitfy it (she brought out sea urchin instead of eel--when we brought it to her attention, she did not remove the unwanted, uneaten item from our bill), AND there was a long hair in one of our rolls! At most sushi establishments, they bring out the items as they are prepared, but here, we had to wait a fairly long time before  being served, and then it was everything, all at once.  Plus, i really like it when the meal commences with a nice, warm hand towel and some complimentary edaname--typical of most sushi places, but NOT here. Overall, a very unpleasant, unappetizing, unsatisfying gastronomical experience!""}, {"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2008-06-02 15:01:40", "review_text": "This is a nice place to sit outside on State St.  I was a tad bit early for sushi (they don't start making sushi until 5:30), so I decided on their Warm Spinach Salad instead.  It was deeeelish.  I had a blackberry martini to sip on, which was also really good.  The server was really nice and attentive the entire time.  

I've also been here previously and have sat in their outside area upstairs, which is also nice.  

I'm curious to try their sushi soon, which might alter my rating."}]}

{"name": "Pacific Crêpes", "address": "705 Anacapa St", "city": "Santa Barbara", "state": "CA", "categories": "Wine Bars, Restaurants, Gluten-Free, French, Bars, Nightlife, Creperies", "hours": {"Monday": "10:0-15:0", "Tuesday": "10:0-15:0", "Wednesday": "10:0-15:0", "Thursday": "10:0-15:0", "Friday": "10:0-15:0", "Saturday": "9:0-15:0", "Sunday": "9:0-15:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "free", "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "Music": false, "Ambience": {"romantic": false, "intimate": false, "touristy": false, "hipster": false, "divey": false, "classy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 3.5, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2019-09-21 13:12:45", "review_text": "All their salads are good but my daughter and I loved the Monaco and Celtic salad the best,  and they also have a lot of choices for crepes. Great food, good customer service and reasonable price...I will definitely recommend this place! Keep it up, Pacific Crepes!"}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2019-02-17 21:29:46", "review_text": "We will miss Pacific Crêpes. They were the real thing. The owners were from Brittany, France. When the mother worked there she ONLY spoke French, even if the customers couldn't. I still don't know how much English she could speak. They hosted our French conversation group for many years (we now meet Wednesdays at Arnoldi's; if you speak a little français come join us). Au revoir, PC!"}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2018-11-26 06:51:57", "review_text": "Delicious and unique french cafe.  Wonderful service.  Amazing coffee too.  Try coffee Mocca.

Enjoy!

We will be back!"}]}

{"name": "Wine + Beer", "address": "38 W Victoria St, Shop 113", "city": "Santa Barbara", "state": "CA", "categories": "Wine Bars, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Wineries, Arts & Entertainment, Food, Nightlife, Bars, Beer Bar", "hours": {"Monday": "11:0-21:0", "Tuesday": "11:0-21:0", "Wednesday": "11:0-18:0", "Thursday": "11:0-22:0", "Friday": "11:0-22:0", "Saturday": "11:0-22:0", "Sunday": "11:0-21:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": true, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": null, "OutdoorSeating": null, "WiFi": null, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": null, "Music": null, "Ambience": null}, "business_stars": 4.5, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2020-06-28 06:19:43", "review_text": "I just had the best 10 minutes of the past two weeks at Beer and Wine.

Ben, who helped me select wines from 3 continents was the most personable, polite and professional person I have met in a long time.

He really knows his stuff!"}, {"review_stars": 1.0, "review_date": "2020-01-27 15:55:18", "review_text": "I would skip this place - limited selection, careless service and pricey.  Much better options to grab a beer or glass of wine all over Santa Barbara.  It is unfortunate because the Public Market is a great, fun place for lunch and dinner."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2019-10-04 20:53:47", "review_text": "Great place to have a drink with a meal from the public market.  Nice selection of beers and wine on tap.  Had a couple free samples to help us decide.  Great local wines, and a not so local sour!"}]}

{"name": "Dogtown", "address": "888 Embarcadero Del N", "city": "Isla Vista", "state": "CA", "categories": "Hot Dogs, Restaurants", "hours": {"Monday": "11:0-22:0", "Tuesday": "11:0-22:0", "Wednesday": "11:0-22:0", "Thursday": "11:0-3:0", "Friday": "11:0-3:0", "Saturday": "11:0-3:0", "Sunday": "11:0-22:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": null, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "Music": null, "Ambience": {"romantic": false, "intimate": false, "classy": false, "hipster": false, "divey": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 4.0, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2012-06-28 16:27:59", "review_text": "Had a BBQ Burger and Crisscut fries from this location which was very delicious. However, this restaurant is no longer here and is being replaced with The Habit Burger [!!!!]."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2012-06-14 00:40:03", "review_text": "This is my favorite place in Isla Vista hands down.  Not only are the hotdogs/sausages great but their burgers are surprisingly the cheapest and most delicious in town!  It does not end there, the sweet potatoe fries are AMAZINGLY delicious, affordable and plentiful!"}, {"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2012-04-11 03:18:49", "review_text": "This place was a go-to when I lived in Isla Vista.  I'd always go for hotdog, sourkraut and mustard, simple and delicious. 

What really sets this place a part from your average hot-dog joint are the dogtown fries.  Think of them as Nacho fries.  They are so amazing.  The fries are loaded with beans, guacamole, onions, jalapenos, grated cheese, & bacon bits.  

These alone give them 4/5 stars. The missing star is the price (but really, what isn't over priced in Isla Vista) and for being a hot dog place, I really wish the hot dogs were amazing instead of okay."}]}

