If I lived closer, this would be a regular spot."}, {"review_stars": 3.0, "review_date": "2015-05-29 06:16:17", "review_text": "Decent coffee at an okay price. Some people like the decorations but I thought it was kind of messy and had a grandma-esque vibe too it. 

I got my usual, an iced coffee and HOT DAMN. It was strong...like a too strong for my tastes. I will come back to try their other drinks though. Not giving up on this place just yet!"}]}

{"name": "The Blue Owl", "address": "5 W Canon Perdido", "city": "Santa Barbara", "state": "CA", "categories": "Food, American (New), Thai, Restaurants, Asian Fusion, Desserts, Cafes, Sandwiches, Caterers, Event Planning & Services", "hours": {"Tuesday": "11:0-20:0", "Wednesday": "11:0-20:0", "Thursday": "11:0-20:0", "Friday": "11:0-2:30", "Saturday": "11:0-2:30", "Sunday": "11:0-20:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": true, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "free", "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "Music": null, "Ambience": {"touristy": false, "hipster": true, "romantic": false, "divey": false, "intimate": false, "trendy": null, "upscale": false, "classy": true, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 4.5, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 3.0, "review_date": "2022-01-19 05:49:47", "review_text": "I got a tofu banh mi, and it was pretty disappointing. The sandwich was fairly small for the price, and the inside of the sandwich was basically empty. Like, if you looked at it from the side, you would think it was just a piece of bread sliced down the middle. Seriously!

To add insult to injury, it tastes *nothing* like a banh mi. They should just call it something else because there was nothing inside that sandwich that tasted anything remotely like a banh mi does.

Three stars because my friend got a turkey sandwich that they really loved, so just averaging out the stars between the two of us."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2022-01-16 18:03:45", "review_text": "This place slaps! I've lived in SB for 5 years and I hit Blue owls all the time. 10/10 would recommend. Fav is the Rice with pork and spicy chili sauce!"}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2022-01-14 00:35:57", "review_text": "What a great little lunch spot! We dropped by one afternoon and were really pleasantly surprised but the quality of the food. Reasonably priced as well, if you factor in the Santa Barbara "tax". The beet salad was really fresh and flavorful, and don't forget to throw an egg on top of that fried rice! Did I mention they serve beer? Not that you would ever have one during lunchtime..."}]}
